- Verified manual anchors from Documents/tm4c129xnczad.pdf:
  - Section 5.2.6 System Control on page 239 states that peripheral-specific RCGCx, SCGCx, and DCGCx registers control clock gating in Run, Sleep, and Deep-Sleep mode, respectively, and places those families at offsets 0x600, 0x700, and 0x800.
  - The same page recommends polling the peripheral-ready PRx register because changes in RCGCx/SCGCx/DCGCx/PCx/SRx may not take effect immediately.
  - Section 5.2.6.3 Deep-Sleep Mode on page 240 states that peripherals are clocked from peripheral-specific DCGC registers when auto-clock gating is enabled, or from RCGC registers when auto-clock gating is disabled.
  - Table 5-11 System Control Register Map on page 250 begins the RCGCx family at offset 0x600 with RCGCWD and continues on page 251.
  - Table 5-11 on page 252 begins the DCGCx family at offset 0x800 with DCGCWD.
